Compute the guide window instead of defaulting. Minimal, faithful fix in the handler (crates/hermit-api/src/handlers/live_tv.rs:52-54):

  async fn get_guide_info(RequireAuth(_auth): RequireAuth) -> Json<GuideInfo> {
      let start = Utc::now();
      let end = start + chrono::Duration::days(GUIDE_DAYS_DEFAULT);
      Json(GuideInfo { start_date: start, end_date: end })
  }

where GUIDE_DAYS_DEFAULT = 7 mirrors Jellyfin's GetGuideDays() fallback (add `use chrono::Utc;`). The cleaner port is to add `async fn get_guide_info(&self) -> Result<GuideInfo, ServiceError>` to the `LiveTvManager` trait (crates/hermit-traits/src/stubs/live_tv.rs) and implement it in HermitLiveTvManager, reading the configured GuideDays (clamped to 1..=14, default 7) from the Live TV options and returning now / now+days; then have the handler call `state.live_tv` (falling back to the default-7 computation when the manager is absent, matching the existing get_live_tv_info pattern at lines 43-46). Note: GuideDays (default 7) is a magic number that mirrors Jellyfin's built-in default — worth surfacing to the user as a candidate config value (valid range 1..=14) rather than hardcoding, per repo config conventions.

Replace `#[derive(...Default...)]` on ListingsProviderInfo (live_tv.rs:622) with a hand-written `impl Default` that mirrors the Jellyfin C# constructor:

impl Default for ListingsProviderInfo {
    fn default() -> Self {
        Self {
            id: None, type_: None, username: None, password: None,
            listings_id: None, zip_code: None, country: None, path: None,
            enabled_tuners: Vec::new(),
            enable_all_tuners: true,
            news_categories: Some(vec!["news","journalism","documentary","current affairs"].into_iter().map(String::from).collect()),
            sports_categories: Some(vec!["sports","basketball","baseball","football"].into_iter().map(String::from).collect()),
            kids_categories: Some(vec!["kids","family","children","childrens","disney"].into_iter().map(String::from).collect()),
            movie_categories: Some(vec!["movie"].into_iter().map(String::from).collect()),
            channel_mappings: Vec::new(),
            movie_prefix: None, preferred_language: None, user_agent: None,
        }
    }
}

Drop `Default` from the derive list (keep Debug/Clone/PartialEq/Eq/Serialize/Deserialize/ToSchema); the `#[serde(default)]` container attr can stay. The handler at live_tv.rs:529 needs no change since it already emits `ListingsProviderInfo::default()`. Note the existing round-trip test at live_tv.rs:1062 still passes (it round-trips serde, doesn't assert the empty default).
